WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.634
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.634
"The Tonight Show," everybody.
You're here.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.834
You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:09.300
What a beautiful fall day
we had today, huh?

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.701
Wasn't it gorgeous?
When I woke up,

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.667
there was a baby sparrow
nesting in my beard.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:13.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:15.534
Guys, I'm very excited about
this.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:17.334
Jack Harlow is my co-host
tonight.

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:22.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.601
He's a stud.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.901
Yeah, he also had the song of
the year, "First Class."

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:29.234
Everyone loves that.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:30.734
Everyone loves that song.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:33.067
Meanwhile, Spirit Airlines is
like, "Eh, it's not relatable."

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.467
Spirit Airlines,
the subway in the sky.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:38.234
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:39.601
Hey, guys, let's get to
some news.

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:40.767
People are talking about this.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.734
Yesterday President Biden went
down to Florida,

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:45.701
and during his visit, he was
caught on a hot microphone

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.100
talking to a local mayor.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.801
Check this out. This is real.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:00.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.701
Biden basically has two modes --

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.801
sweet grandpa
and Tarantino movie.

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:06.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:08.467
Biden sounds like
a hard-nosed P.I.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:09.701
who wraps up cases by saying...

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:17.567
♪♪

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:23.434
♪♪

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:24.934
Actually, Biden didn't stop
there.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.601
He actually kept talking.
-Really?

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:28.234
-Yeah, we got exclusive footage.
Listen to this.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:29.601
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.934
Wow.

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:47.067
♪♪

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:51.100
-Some big news. Today, President
Biden pardoned all people

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.200
convicted of possessing
marijuana under federal law.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.601
Signaling a major step towards
legalization.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.934
I'm pretty sure Biden's approval
rating is about

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:06.334
to get high for the first time.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:10.067
[ Laughter ]
-Whoa!

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:12.634
-Yeah, the President cancelled
student-loan debt.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.701
And now he's pardoning people
for weed.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.634
I think Biden's going to be able
to get into any frat

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:19.567
he wants right now.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.634
Meanwhile, I have a feeling
Trump is about to claim that all

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:23.868
his classified documents
were just rolling papers.

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.367
Speaking of the former
president, yesterday Trump was

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.501
delivering remarks
when he brought up the FBI's

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:30.934
search of Mar-a-Lago.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:33.100
And he's definitely looking
for the bright side here.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.267
Take a look.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:35.567
-Has anyone heard about
the document hopes

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:38.634
helicopters flying over
Mar-a-Lago?

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.667
Well, they've given us
about $5 billion worth

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:43.067
of free publicity, I will say.

00:02:43.067 --> 00:02:45.100
People say,
"That's a nice house."

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.901
If it weren't so nice, they
probably wouldn't be doing it

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.400
because, you know,
it gets ratings.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.367
When they look, they say,
"that's a beautiful place."

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.267
-Right now, Trump's watching
the Jeffrey Dahmer show like,

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.868
"Well, great publicity."

00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:00.200
[ Laughter ]
"Really is.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.601
A lot of people are watching
that show."

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.367
Listen to this.
I read that the Air Force just

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:06.634
announced a plan to reduce
their carbon footprint

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:08.934
and adapt to climate change.

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.801
Yeah, it's a major move.
In fact, the Air Force just

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.367
unveiled their new F-24 Prius.
Have you seen this?

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:15.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.868
Guys, today marked the start of
New York Comic-Con.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:19.701
Yeah.
[ Cheers ]

00:03:19.701 --> 00:03:22.300
They're expecting
over 150,000 fans,

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.968
and a lot of them will be
in costume.

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.367
So we thought it would be
helpful to point out

00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.000
the differences between
a New York Comic-Con Spider-Man

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.534
and a Times Square Spider-Man.

00:03:29.534 --> 00:03:31.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:35.133
For instance, Comic-Con
Spider-Man just paid 125 bucks

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:36.467
for a ticket to get in.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:39.167
Times Square Spider-Man
just paid 125 bucks

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:40.434
of bail to get out.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:43.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:47.300
Next up, Comic-Con Spider-Man
wants to score with Mary Jane.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.133
Times Square Spider-Man already
scored some Mary Jane.

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.067
Next up, Comic-Con Spider-Man

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.701
wears an official spandex suit
he bought online.

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:58.067
Times Square Spider-Man wears

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:00.667
a homemade suit that's part
Spanx, part Skims.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:01.901
He calls them skanks.

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.601
And finally, Comic-Con
Spider-Man waits

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:08.067
for the bathroom in a long line.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:10.501
Times Square Spider-Man goes to
the bathroom in his skanks.

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.067
[ Laughter ]
That's the difference.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.934
Guys, get this, I heard that
the U.S. might start requiring

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:19.901
beer, wine, and spirits makers
to provide more information

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.901
on what's in their drinks.

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.300
These are strange times.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.400
Weed is about to be legal,
but we need a full report

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.734
on what's in Bud Light Lime.

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:28.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.968
Guys, finally, a house
in Michigan is going viral

00:04:30.968 --> 00:04:33.000
after the owner synced up
his Halloween lights

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.767
to the tune of a song
from "Hocus Pocus 2."

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.067
Watch this.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:40.834
-♪ One way or another,
we're gonna find ya ♪

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:43.567
♪ We're gonna get ya, get ya,
get ya, get ya, one way ♪

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.167
-Yeah, it seems annoying,

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.300
